    #!/usr/bin/env bash
    # Milestone 1 part 8 P1 negative.log (specs/0015-open-checks.md, "### P1" and
    # "The open-check library"). Two families, every fixture generated:
    #
    # (S) scripts/edit-open-check.sh, the four cases "### P1" names, each on a
    #     keep directory this log builds from generated workbooks:
    #       S1 a planted output that cannot open (a truncated archive): lo fail,
    #          listed as a finding, exit 1;
    #       S2 a planted input that cannot open: listed among the refused inputs,
    #          exit 0;
    #       S3 an image that is not there: error, listed among the checks that did
    #          not run, exit 2;
    #       S4 an empty keep directory: refused, exit 2, no record and no reasons
    #          directory;
    #     and two refusals beyond the four, each a one-line check with no
    #     container: S5 half a pair, S6 a record already there. Each record's
    #     .txt rows are compared, row by row, with the bytes and sha256 this log
    #     computes from the keep's files, and its header with the script's own
    #     constant, read from the script at the phase commit.
    # (R) the runner's T3 P3 negative cases rerun on the moved library ("the
    #     runner's behaviour is unchanged, shown by T3 P3's negative cases rerun
    #     on it (ok, fail, error on the same fixtures)"). The fixtures are T3 P3's:
    #     its generator is read out of records/logs/t3-p3/negative.log, where its
    #     script is printed, not retyped. The open-check cases C1 to C9, C11 and
    #     C12 run twice on the same scratch corpus and the same binaries: once
    #     with the runner at the phase commit (the main tree's, which sources
    #     scripts/lo-check.sh) and once with the runner at the part 7 close-out
    #     record commit (in a detached worktree; lo_check still inline there).
    #     Each case's T3 P3 assertion is made on both, and the two runs' outcome,
    #     lo and lo_in columns and their reason files are compared byte for byte.
    #     C10 (the record script) and M1 to M4 (the conversion run directly) do
    #     not run lo_check and are not rerun.
    #
    # WRITTEN FOR M1 part 8 P1 from part 7 P2's negative script (printed in
    # records/logs/m1p7-p2/negative.log) and T3 P3's (printed in
    # records/logs/t3-p3/negative.log). From part 7 P2's: lines 1 to 3, the shape
    # greps with controls, the roles by subject, the rerun block, SERIALIZED,
    # the root lines, the counting controls. From T3 P3's: the generator (read,
    # not copied), the case list C1 to C9, C11, C12 and each case's assertion.
    # What differs, and why:
    #  1. The phase, the log directory and the subjects are part 8 P1's.
    #  2. The xlsx-diff cases and the record script's family B are gone: this
    #     phase changes neither. Family S is new; family R is T3 P3's cases run
    #     on two runners and compared.
    #  3. T3 P3 required a clean tree; this log allows this phase's logs, its
    #     record pair and planning's uncommitted specs/0015, and nothing else.
    #  4. The build directory is on the disk, <home>/.cache/emend-build/
    #     m1p8-p1-negative, not in /tmp, a tmpfs that filled during gate.log's
    #     first attempt; the base runner's worktree lives there too.
    #  5. The script's reasons directories are made under <scratch>/w by setting
    #     TMPDIR per case, so S4 can show none was made.
    #
    # RERUN AFTER INDEPENDENT CHECK 1 (same phase commit): F6, the <repo> root
    # line said scripts/lo-check.sh is run from it; it is sourced by the runner
    # and the script, never run, and the line now says so. Nothing else changed.
    #
    # Usage: m1p8-p1-negative.sh <phase commit> > <scratch file>; the caller moves
    # the output to records/logs/m1p8-p1/negative.log.
    set -uo pipefail
    SELF_DIR=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)
    SELF=$SELF_DIR/$(basename "$0")
    cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)" || exit 2
    MAIN=$(pwd)
